Where a shelter admits minors, the House Rules shall contain a provision detailing the shelter's policy regarding minor residents including that:

(1) Minor residents, who are under the age of 17, shall be supervised at all times by a parent, a guardian, or a qualified staff member;

(2) The owner(s) of the shelter shall not allow minor residents, who are under the age of 17, to sleep in areas which accommodate adult residents outside of each minor resident's immediate family without assigning at least one staff member to monitor such minor resident, and that in order to facilitate monitoring by an assigned staff member, each minor resident should be placed in close proximity to his or her respective family and to other minor residents or families with minor residents;

(3) The owner(s) and/or operator(s) of a shelter shall:

 (a) Ensure that all school age minor residents are enrolled in, and have the opportunity to attend, school as required under Michigan law;

 (b) Provide space and time to enable school age minor residents to complete homework assignments; and

 (c) Cooperate with parents, guardians, and appropriate school personnel to promote the educational needs of school age minor residents; and

(4) The owner(s) and/or operator(s) of a shelter shall make every effort to provide minor residents with recreational activities and facilities that are separate from those for adult residents.

(R 36.602; Part 6, Sec. B, eff. 4-4-1997)

**R 36.1201.**

The House Rules shall inform residents that the shelter's staff members are trained and knowledgeable in:

(1) First-aid;

(2) Fire and emergency procedures including, but not limited to, the proper use of a fire extinguisher;

(3) Resident complaint and grievance procedures;

(4) Special needs of the homeless and of victims of domestic violence;

(5) Resident confidentiality requirements; and

(6) The appropriate chains of authority or command within the shelter.

(R 36.1201; Part 12, eff. 4-4-1997)

**R 36.1401.**

The House Rules shall contain a provision that shall inform residents of their responsibilities while residing in the shelter.

(R 36.1401; Part 14, Sec. A, eff. 4-4-1997)

**R 36.1402.**

At a minimum, the House Rules provision regarding residents' responsibilities shall contain the following:

"You have a responsibility:

(1) To comply with the House Rules;

(2) To cooperate with directions and instructions given by staff members of the shelter;

(3) To pay any required escrow or other fee unless you are financially unable to do so;

(4) Not to possess, either within or outside of the shelter, any alcoholic beverages, illegal drugs, drug paraphernalia, or weapons of any kind including, but not limited to, firearms, air guns, knives and darts;

(5) Not to disturb or to annoy other residents through unnecessary noise or boisterous conduct;

(6) To keep the general areas, and your space, clean and tidy;

(7) To supervise and monitor any minor resident if you are their parent or guardian;

(8) To enroll any minor resident in school and require the minor resident to complete homework assignments if you are their parent or guardian;

(9) To consume food where designated within the shelter;

(10) To inform a staff member that you are taking medication; and

(11) To abide by the shelter's policy regarding smoking."

(R 36.1402; Part 14, Sec. B, eff. 4-4-1997)

(a) Nothing in this Code, including the ordinance that adopts this Code, shall affect any City ordinance that was enacted under the 1954, 1964, and 1984 Detroit City Codes, but under current law, as provided for in Section 4-114 of the Charter, would be adopted through a resolution, including, but not limited to, any such ordinance which:

