(7) The Airport Department may sell and convey or lease, with the approval of the City Council, any of the buildings or land under its control whenever required by the interests of the City;

(8) The Airport Department may make, with the approval of the City Council, all contracts or leases necessary to carry out the objects and purposes of the Airport Department, as provided in this section;

(9) The Airport Department may recommend the enactment of ordinances designed to safeguard the public upon or beyond the limits of public or private airports, heliports, seaplane bases, landing fields or sites or other aeronautical facilities within the City or its police jurisdiction against the perils and hazards attendant to the operation of aircraft and aeronautical facilities, which ordinances shall not be inconsistent with the laws of the federal government and this state or the rules and regulations of the Federal Aviation Administration or the Michigan Department of Transportation Bureau of Aeronautics;

(10) The Airport Department may request such assistance as may be reasonably necessary from other City departments in the performance of its duties; and

(11) The Airport Department shall have the power and authority to specifically delegate any part or all of its power and authority to any person employed in the Airport Department for the accomplishment of the duties with which the Airport Department is charged.

