The Building Official, as defined in Section 8-9-11 of this Code, and designated inspectors of the Department, are authorized:

(1) To inspect and test all equipment that requires a new installation or alteration permit under the provisions of this article;

(2) To semi-annually inspect all escalators, moving walks, and all passenger elevators except private residence elevators, platform lifts and stairway chairlifts, barrier-free lifting devices, and limited-use/limited-application elevators;

(3) To annually inspect all platform lifts and stairway chairlifts, barrier-free lifting devices, and limited-use/limited-application elevators that are installed in other than single-family residential dwelling units;

(4) To annually inspect all freight elevators and all dumbwaiters, except hand-power dumbwaiters, having a capacity of less than 100 pounds and a width of 18 inches or less;

(5) To inspect and test permanent elevators in temporary use, as provided for in Subdivision C of this division, not less than once every 90 days;

(6) To annually inspect and test elevator fire service systems pursuant to Division 6 of this article and the ASME Code;

(7) To annually inspect and test standby or emergency power systems;

(8) To inspect and perform a load test on standby or emergency power systems every five years; and

(9) To make, or cause to be made, such other inspections or tests required by this article and other codes adopted by reference pursuant to Section 8-9-2 of this Code or deemed necessary for the purpose of safety and the enforcement of this article.

