(a) A Temporary Certificate of Use for an elevator being installed for permanent use may be issued before final completion during construction or renovation of the building for carrying workers and their materials, only, or other specific use approved by the Department.

(b) A Temporary Certificate of Use pursuant to this section shall not be issued until the non-refundable fee that is established and approved in accordance with Section 8-9-21 of this Code has been paid to the Department. Where the fee is paid by check or money order, it shall be made payable to the "Treasurer, City of Detroit."

(c) The Temporary Certificate of Use shall be signed by a designated inspector of the Department and shall bear the date of issuance, renewal and expiration, and shall designate the type/class of service allowed. The certificate shall be issued for periods of not more than 90 days. The inspector is authorized to renew the temporary certificate for additional periods of not more than 90 days each.

(d) To be approved for the issuance of a Temporary Certificate of Use during construction, the elevator, and its hoistways and associated spaces, shall meet the requirements of Section 5.10 of the ASME Code, the applicable provisions of this article, and the following additional requirements:

(1) An approved-type governor and car safety;

(2) A car with an approved solid top and sides except at car openings;

(3) An approved hoistway enclosure not less than ten feet high on each floor;

(4) Approved-type doors and gates at least six feet high at all hoistway openings;

(5) A locking device on the hoistway door or gate meeting the requirements of Sections 2.12.2.4 and 2.12.2.4.5 of the ASME Code;

(6) Car safety and terminal stopping devices have been tested, in the presence of a designated inspector of the Department, with rated load in the car to determine whether the devices are in safe and proper operating condition;

(7) An approved temporary hoistway lighting system shall be installed throughout the rise of the hoistway; and

(8) A temporary guard or screen shall be installed throughout the rise of the hoistway where more than one elevator occupies the same hoistway during construction or renovation.

(e) The holder of a Temporary Certificate of Use shall cause the subject elevator to be inspected and serviced at such periods as may be necessary to maintain the equipment in a safe operating condition, but not less than once every 30 days, by an unlimited-elevator journeyperson who is licensed by the City.

(f) Where the capacity of the elevator exceeds 1,500 pounds, an elevator operator shall be in charge of the loading and unloading of the elevator.

(g) A means of voice communication shall be provided between the elevator operator in the car and the station that is located on each landing or floor.

(h) Unless all requirements for permanent use of the elevator are met, the speed of such elevator shall not exceed 600 feet per minute.

