Each elevator operator shall be provided with a copy of the following instructions to be read and applied:

(1) Make a trial trip each morning before carrying passengers;

(2) Report any abnormal operating conditions promptly to the individual in charge;

(3) Do not attempt to make any repair on the elevator without approval;

(4) Carry no passengers or freight while any inspection, repair, or adjustment is in progress and operate the car only in response to directions from the elevator repair person;

(5) Do not move the car when a maintenance person or repair person is in the pit or on top of the car except as such individual may direct;

(6) Do not ride in the elevator or allow any other individual to ride while heavy objects in excess of the rated capacity of the elevator are being carried;

(7) Limit the number of passengers to the rated passenger capacity of the car and do not permit overcrowding;

(8) Where the car should stop suddenly and will not restart, call for the individual in charge and operate the elevator only at his or her direction. Under these circumstances, do not leave the car or allow any other individual to leave a stalled car between landings;

(9) Be familiar with emergency devices located in the car;

(10) Never leave the car in the ordinary course of operation. When going off duty or leaving the car for any reason, even for a few minutes, be sure that the power is disconnected or that the operating mechanism is locked;

(11) Always operate the elevator on designated attendant operations; and

(12) Always leave a hydraulic elevator parked out of service at the lowest landing.

