A designated inspector of the Buildings, Safety Engineering, and Environmental Department shall provide a copy of the following instructions to each operator who shall learn them thoroughly:

(1) Always open the service switch or lock the operating mechanism in or adjacent to the hoist when leaving the hoist unattended;

(2) Be sure the operating mechanism is in the "Stop" position before closing the service switch;

(3) Make a trial trip each morning before carrying passengers;

(4) Report any abnormal operating conditions promptly to the individual in charge;

(5) Repairs or adjustments shall be made only by a person who is licensed by the City as an unlimited-elevator journeyperson;

(6) Carry no passengers or freight while inspections, repairs, or adjustments are in progress;

(7) Do not move the hoist when anyone is in the pit or on top of the hoist;

(8) Do not ride in the hoist or allow others to ride while a heavy object in excess of the rated capacity of the personnel hoist is being carried;

(9) Hoistway doors or gates shall always be in the normally closed and locked position before the hoist is started. The hoist shall be brought to a stop at the landing level before the hoistway door or gate is opened by hand unless an automatic leveling device is provided;

(10) The operating device shall be in the "Stop" position until the hoistway door and hoist gate are in the normally closed position;

(11) Do not allow more than the authorized number of passengers to ride the hoist or permit crowding;

(12) Do not reverse the operating device suddenly; stop before reversing;

(13) Move the operating device to the "Stop" position on approaching a terminal landing without waiting for the terminal stopping devices to come into action;

(14) When the power goes off while the hoist is in motion, move the operating device to the "Stop" position and start the hoist in the usual manner upon return to power;

(15) When the hoist refuses to stop, do not attempt to leave the hoist or permit others to do so. The hoist will be stopped by the application of the safeties if it attains excessive speed of descent or by the automatic terminal stops at either end of the hoistway;

(16) If the hoist should stop suddenly and will not restart, call for the individual in charge and operate the machine only at his or her direction. Do not leave the hoist or permit others to leave a stalled hoist between landings, unless instructed by the individual in charge to do so, and then only if the individual in charge is available to assist the passengers to safely leave the hoist;

(17) If the hoist will not start, return the operating device to the "Stop" position. If the hoist appears overloaded, remove part of the load and try the operating device. If the hoist still will not move, return the operating device to the "Stop" position and notify the individual in charge;

(18) Be familiar with the emergency devices located in the hoist, understand their functions, and know how to operate them; and

(19) Never leave the hoist in the ordinary course of operation. When going off duty or leaving the hoist for any reason, even for a few minutes, be sure that the power is disconnected or that the operating mechanism is locked.

