The duties and responsibilities of the Emergency Management Coordinator shall include:

(1) Coordinating and implementing the City’s emergency operations plan and consulting with other governmental, as well as other public and private agencies, to formulate plans, policies, and operational procedures for emergency preparedness, relief, recovery assistance, and response to any threat to the health and safety of the people of the City and to property located within the City;

(2) Developing plans and procedures for the coordinated utilization of all City resources and facilities of the City for emergency management consistent with the Michigan Emergency Management Act and this chapter;

(3) Coordinating the recruitment of volunteer personnel and agencies to augment City personnel and facilities for emergency management purposes;

(4) Preparing the City’s population for an emergency, in conjunction with other City departments and agencies, through public educational programs;

(5) Conducting public practice alerts and tests to ensure the efficient operation of the Department of Homeland Security, and to familiarize the citizenry with any emergency management regulations and procedures, provided that prior to any such practice alerts and tests, the Emergency Management Coordinator shall notify the City Council in writing, which shall contain the regulations and procedures pertaining thereto;

(6) Coordinating the activity of all public and private agencies comprising the Department of Homeland Security, including coordination of planning and of purchasing of emergency management equipment and supplies for the City;

(7) Negotiating with owners, or persons in possession of buildings or other property, for the use of such buildings or property for emergency management purposes, including, but not limited to, the placement and maintenance of the emergency management system, and the designation of suitable buildings as public shelters;

(8) Assuming such authority and conducting such activity as the Mayor may direct to promote and execute the City’s emergency management plan; and

