It shall be unlawful for any person to operate a massage facility or massage school or to engage in the practice of massage therapy unless such person shall have complied with the following rules and regulations:

(1) Service in massage facilities licensed under this article shall be limited to exercise, baths and massage therapy. Medical treatment of any kind shall not be given to any patron without a prescription from a registered physician. The use of heat lamps and sun-ray lamps only will be permitted;

(2) No person who has any visible symptoms of a communicable disease, such as a rash, discharge or fever or who is complaining of a sore throat may be attended by any licensee under this article or any person engaged in the practice of massage therapy;

(3) Each applicant for an apprentice’s or student’s certificate of registration under this article, or a renewal thereof, shall present a certificate from a registered physician, certifying that the applicant is free from communicable disease;

(4) Advertising that there is a nurse in attendance is prohibited unless there is a registered graduate nurse constantly in attendance during the business hours of the massage facility;

(5) Advertising that there is a doctor in attendance is prohibited unless there is a registered physician constantly in attendance during the business hours of the massage facility;

(6) Licensees shall exercise every precaution for the safety of patrons including watching for early signs of fatigue or weakness and immediately discontinuing whatever form of service is being given upon the appearance of such signs;

(7) No massage facility shall be operated in direct connection with living quarters, unless specifically approved by the Buildings, Safety Engineering, and Environmental Department;

(8) The premises used for a massage facility shall be well lighted and ventilated, shall be kept clean, and the furniture and equipment shall be maintained in a safe and sanitary condition. There shall be an adequate supply of running hot and cold water during business hours. Bathing devices shall be thoroughly cleaned before the use of each patron;

(9) All robes, towels, blankets and linens furnished for the use of one patron shall be thoroughly laundered before being offered to another;

(10) While attending patrons, the conductor, instructor, massage therapist, or apprentice shall be fully clothed in a uniform or a garment made of washable material, and shall be kept in clean condition. The sleeves shall not reach below the elbow;

(11) The skin of the hands of those attending patrons shall be clean and in healthy condition and the nails shall be kept short. The hands shall be washed thoroughly before giving the patron any attention;

(12) Licensees shall be restricted in the exercise of their license to the places set forth in their certificate, provided, that the giving of massage therapy, baths, and exercise in the patron’s place of residence is permitted; and

(13) The private parts of patrons must be covered when in the presence of a conductor, massage therapist, or instructor. Any contact with a patron’s genital area is prohibited.

