Licensees under this article shall be subject to the following rules and regulations:

(1) Patrons with symptoms of communicable disease, etc. No person who has any visible symptom of a communicable disease, such as a rash, discharge or fever or who is complaining of a sore throat may be attended by any licensee, attendant or employee;

(2) Separate sections for persons of opposite sex. There shall be separate sections in the public bathhouse for men and women. Serving or attending therein of patrons of the opposite sex is prohibited;

(3) Physical examination of employee, etc. All applicants for licenses under this article, attendants or employees, shall first register with the Health Department and must present a certificate from a licensed physician certifying freedom from communicable disease. The Health Department may require, from time to time, but not more than once every 12 months, the applicant, attendants and employees either to submit to physical examinations and laboratory examination or to furnish a certificate from a licensed physician embodying such requirements;

(4) Bathhouses in living quarters prohibited. No public bathhouse shall be conducted in direct connection with living quarters;

(5) Sanitation. The premises used for public bathhouses shall be kept well lighted and ventilated. They shall be kept clean, and the furniture and equipment shall be maintained in a safe and sanitary condition. There shall be an adequate supply of running hot and cold water during business hours. Bathing devices shall be thoroughly cleansed before use by the patron;

(6) Laundering of linens, etc. All robes, towels, blankets and linens furnished for the use of one patron shall be thoroughly laundered before being offered to another;

(7) Uniforms of attendants. Uniforms or garments worn by those attending patrons shall be of washable material and shall be kept in a clean condition. The sleeves shall not reach below the elbow;

(8) Hands of attendants. The skin of the hands of those attending patrons shall be clean and in healthy condition and the nails shall be kept short. The hands will be washed thoroughly before giving the patron any attention; and

(9) Location. Licensees under this article shall be restricted in the operation of a public bathhouse to the place set forth in the license.

