(a) A business may apply for and receive certification as a Detroit-Based Business, a Detroit-Based Small Business, a Detroit-Headquartered Business, Detroit-Resident Business, a Minority-Owned Business Enterprise, and Women-Owned Business Enterprise and receive certification as follows:

(1) A business that qualifies as a Detroit-Based Small Business will receive certification as a Detroit-Based Small Business and, where determined to be headquartered in Detroit, as a Detroit-Headquartered Business; and

(2) A business that qualifies as a Detroit-Headquartered Business will receive certification as a Detroit-Headquartered Business, but not as a Detroit-Based Business;

(3) A business that qualifies as a Detroit-Resident Business will receive certification as a Detroit-Resident Business, but not as a Detroit-Based Business;

(4) A business that does not qualify as a Detroit-Headquartered Business or as a Detroit-Based Small Business may receive certification as a Detroit-Based Business.

(b) A certification for a Detroit-Based Business shall be for a term of two years from the date of certification. In the event that a business files an application for certification as a Detroit-Headquartered Business, or for certification as a Detroit-Based Small Business, after receiving certification as a Detroit-Based Business, the expiration date certification as a Detroit-Headquartered Business or as a Detroit-Based Small Business shall correspond with the expiration date of its certification as Detroit-Based Business. Where information changes or a complaint is filed, the City reserves the right to request the follow-up documentation from a particular business.

It shall be unlawful for any educational institution:

(1) To discriminate against an individual in the full utilization of or benefit from the institution, or the services, activities, or programs provided by the institution because of race, color, religious beliefs, national origin, age, height, weight, familial status, marital status, disability, sex, sexual orientation, or gender identity or expression;

(2) To exclude, expel, limit, or otherwise discriminate against an individual seeking admission as a student or an individual enrolled as a student in the terms, conditions, or privileges of the institution, because of race, color, religious beliefs, national origin, age, height, weight, familial status, marital status, disability, sex, sexual orientation, or gender identity or expression;

(3) For purposes of admission only, to make or use a written or oral inquiry or form of application that elicits or attempts to elicit information concerning the race, color, religious beliefs, national origin, age, height, weight, familial status, marital status, disability, sex, sexual orientation, or gender identity or expression of a person, except as permitted by rule of the Human Rights Commission or as required by federal law, rule, or regulation, or pursuant to an affirmative action program;

(4) To print or publish or cause to be printed or published a catalog, notice, or advertisement indicating a preference, limitation, specification, or discrimination based on the race, color, religious beliefs, national origin, age, height, weight, familial status, marital status, disability, sex, sexual orientation, or gender identity or expression of an applicant for admission to the educational institution; or

