(5) Notifying the Michigan Public Service Commission when the Director of the Department of Public Works has granted or denied a permit in accordance with Section 45-2-6(a) of this Code;

(6) Not unreasonably denying an application for a permit in accordance with Section 45-2-6(a) of this Code;

(7) Issuing a permit in the form approved by the Michigan Public Service Commission, with or without additional or different permit terms, as provided for in Section 45-2-6(b) of this Code;

(8) Limiting the conditions imposed on the issuance of a permit to the telecommunications provider’s access and usage of the public right-of-way in accordance with Section 45-2-6(c) of this Code;

(9) Not requiring a bond of a telecommunications provider which exceeds the reasonable cost to ensure that the public right-of-way is returned to its original condition during and after the telecommunication provider’s access and usage in accordance with Section 45-2-6(d) of this Code;

