A shared electric personal mobility device must be constructed and maintained in accordance with the following standards:

(1) The shared electric personal mobility device is constructed of durable and impact-resistant materials that are safe for outdoor use and are in compliance with all federal and state safety standards, including any such standards promulgated by the U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission or the State of Michigan, or are contained in this division;

(2) The shared electric personal mobility device's exterior surfaces are clean and free of damage or excessive wear;

(3) The shared electric personal mobility device's battery should be rated IP68 or higher. All such equipment must be free of damage or excessive wear;

(4) The shared electric personal mobility device's wheels, including their axles, hubs and spokes, are securely attached, in alignment, and free of damage or excessive wear;

(5) The shared electric personal mobility device's wheels are equipped with rubberized tires, either solid or pneumatic, that are suitable for use on paved surfaces and that are in compliance with Section 662(5) of the Michigan Vehicle Code, being MCL 257.662(5). All pneumatic tires are inflated to recommended pressures;

(6) The shared electric personal mobility device is equipped with fenders that are free of damage or excessive wear;

