(a) When a shared electric personal mobility device is parked in a public place, it must be parked in accordance with Section 660d of the Michigan Vehicle Code, being MCL 257.660d, as well as the additional standards set forth in this section. The operator of the electric personal mobility device is responsible for adherence to all such standards.

(b) A shared electric personal mobility device must not be parked in a manner that could foreseeably impose a threat to public health and safety, including the health and safety of proximate pedestrians, vehicles, and property.

(c) A docked shared electric personal mobility device must be parked in a designated docking station if any such station is within a reasonable vicinity and has available capacity.

(d) The Director of the Department of Public Works may designate zones in which electric personal mobility device parking is expressly authorized and may take all necessary steps to identify and enforce such zones through, fencing, geofencing, signage, striping, or other means. In all circumstances in which Subsection (c) of this section does not apply, an electric personal mobility device must be parked in a designated parking zone if any such zone is within a reasonable vicinity and has available capacity.

(e) In all circumstances in which Subsections (c) and (d) of this section do not apply, the shared electric personal mobility device must be parked in accordance with the following standards, as applicable:

(1) The shared electric personal mobility device is parked on the sidewalk, fully contained within the "furniture zone" of the sidewalk corridor;

(2) The shared electric personal mobility device is parked freestanding in an upright position and is not leaning against or fastened to a stationary structure or object not designated for such purpose, including bus shelters, fences, fire hydrants, light poles, mailboxes, sign posts, street furniture, street trees and traffic signals, but excluding bicycle racks or docking stations;

